WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:10.120
Hi, welcome back to the Lam Rim (LAM RIM). This is episode five,

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:13.860
and it's called "Read the Recipe."

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:24.040
I chose... the first image I chose is a small girl and she's sort of protecting a small plant.

00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:32.140
To me this picture, which looks 
like Nick's daughter actually, Amalie, right?

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:39.000
She's protecting this plant with her hands 
and what it means is it's very important...

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:44.070
if you're a gardener, it's very important to 
take care of a plant when it's young.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:53.980
In the first week or two you really, really have to pay attention. You have to water very regularly,

00:00:54.340 --> 00:01:00.300
and you have to really protect the plant from wind,
and from birds, and from deer, and things like that.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:03.719
So that's going to be a theme in this first part here.

00:01:04.300 --> 00:01:12.720
de na chu sab sabmo dang gya chenpoy ke drak chen shen ma gya cher ma jung na-ang
DES NA CHOS ZAB ZAB MO DANG RGYA CHEN PO'I SKAD GRAGS CAN GZHAN MA
RGYA CHER MA BYUNG NA'ANG,)

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:19.380
So look, some people get really attracted to big, big Dharma teachings.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:21.520
They get to go to an initiation.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.650
It's super secret.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:29.879
The lama says, "I'm going to teach you something that no one ever gets to hear and this is a special initiation," or

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:38.200
"This is some special emptiness thing, emptiness level seventeen; I never teach it to anybody."

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:47.580
So, we get all excited and we all say,
"Oh, let's go! The lama's going to teach emptiness level seventeen."

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:55.480
ke drak chen (SKAD GRAGS CAN) means, you've heard 
these famous names like Mahamudra (mahāmudrā) or 
Dzogchen (RDZOGS CHEN), and you get all excited.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:02:02.420
gya cher ma jung na-ang (RGYA CHER MA BYUNG NA'ANG)--he says forget the big Dharma teachings, you know, don't worry so much about the big Dharma teachings.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.460
rang rang gi gyu kyi ge tsul long gi dompa lekpar sung na--
(RANG RANG GI RGYUD KYI DGE TSUL SLONG GI SDOM PA LEGS PAR BSRUNG NA,)

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:15.840
if you just take care of the small beautiful 
vows you have in your own heart.

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.980
Just take care of them.

00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:23.000
sung na... rang re dendun du chepay che chu sundro--
(BSRUNG NA, RANG RE DGE 'DUN DU BYED PA'I BYED CHOS SU 'GRO,)

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:32.480
then you have created the Sangha (saṃgha). It's an unusual expression. You are creating Sangha.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.180
You are upholding the Sangha.

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:40.620
You are sustaining the Buddhist community in the world

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:45.474
if you just take care of your baby 
vows that the lama gave you.

00:02:45.474 --> 00:02:46.859
Be nice to other people.

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.529
Take care of this small plant.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.360
Take care of this small plant.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.460
I like to call it your future barrel of peaches.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:01.679
It means, recently I did plant a peach tree. In fact today, I was taking care of it and

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:10.200
it started out as a tiny, little plant and you take care of it and you take care of it, and then if you take good care of it...

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.020
in fact, my first peaches came out today.

00:03:15.010 --> 00:03:19.529
You will get millions of peaches, 
thousands of peaches. So just,

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:25.589
don't worry about some big famous Dharma teaching, some big famous initiation.

00:03:25.590 --> 00:03:30.750
Don't worry about it. 
Get your little ten vows from your lama and

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:39.380
plant that seed and take care of it, and then that's 
going to give you thousands, millions of fruits.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:47.360
Don't worry about it. Enjoy the small thing, take care of it, and it's going to bring you a million things.

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:50.860
rang re gendun du chepay, tenpa dzinpa yang de nyi yin--
(RANG RE DGE 'DUN DU BYED PA'I, BSTAN PA 'DZIN PA YANG DE NYID YIN,)

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:53.560
and then you are a Buddhist master; we talked about that idea already.

00:03:53.562 --> 00:03:58.290
He says, "You want to be a Buddhist master,  
you want to be a master meditator?

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.950
Protect your small vows, be nice to other people."

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:06.440
Share your coffee with your friends.

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:09.720
Open the door for somebody else.

00:04:09.820 --> 00:04:14.840
Give a roll of toilet paper to your neighbor during the virus.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.200
Take care of the small things--
they become the big things.

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:24.180
ge tsul long gi dompa sok ta chi--
(DGE TSUL SLONG GI SDOM PA SOGS LTA CI,)

00:04:24.820 --> 00:04:34.300
I'm not even talking, he says... his audience was a lot of geshes (DGE BSHES), a lot of tulkus (SPRUL SKU), and a lot of senior monks.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:40.180
The audience of this lama, when he gave this teaching-- 
I guess in the 1920s, something like that--

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:49.600
the audience were very, very high Buddhist monks, lamas, incarnated lamas.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:57.100
He says forget these heavy vows that you guys have, let's talk about the vows--
kyimpa sok kyi kyang nyen ne kyi dompa 
(KHYIM PA SOGS KYIS KYANG BSNYEN GNAS KYI SDOM PA)

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:00.620
let's talk about the one-day vow

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:09.040
that a normal family person takes. A normal village person in a small village in Tibet.

00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:18.380
And let's say, I don't know, they work as a 
sheep herder and they just get a one-day vow.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:22.700
So forget these big monk's vows and super monk's vows.

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:29.220
Let's talk about these modest 
vows that everybody starts with.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:31.840
nyin chik tsam sung na-ang
(NYIN GCIG TZAM BSRUNG NA'ANG)

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:34.020
Even if you just keep them for one day,

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:40.060
pen yun chewa dulwa lung dang, do dzang lun sok su ngun gyi chungway lo gyu selwa tar yin
(PHAN YON CHE BA 'DUL BA LUNG DANG, MDO MDZANGS BLUN SOGS SU SNGON GYI BYUNG BA'I LO RGYUS GSAL BA LTAR YIN,)

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:45.320
Then there are many, many stories in the great books. dulwa lung ('DUL BA LUNG)

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:47.640
means "Vinaya scriptures."

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:52.820
do dzang lun (MDO MDZANGS BLUN) is a very famous sutra called the "Sutra of the Wise and the Foolish."

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:55.660
And he says you can read those sutras and

00:05:56.229 --> 00:06:02.879
you will read beautiful stories about people who kept their tiny vows and had extraordinary results.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:09.539
de na, nyen ne dang, ge nyen, de-ang na shi, na sum, na chik sok lo nu chi yud kyi sung chi tub che
(DES NA, BSNYEN GNAS DANG, DGE BSNYEN, DE'ANG SNA BZHI, SNA GSUM, SNA GCIG SOGS BLO NUS CI YOD KYIS BSRUNG CI THUB BYED,)

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:19.720
So take those one-day vows, keep them as 
well as you can, take baby monks vows.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:27.140
Take your... you can take lifetime layman's vows.

00:06:27.260 --> 00:06:28.720
Now,

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:35.920
the lifetime layman's vow in its complete form has five parts. And it's very, very basic.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:43.160
I will not kill a human being or a human fetus. 
That's the first one.

00:06:43.940 --> 00:06:51.320
Number two, I will not steal anything that's more valuable than about ten U.S. dollars.

00:06:51.680 --> 00:06:54.140
Something that has some value, I will not steal.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:07:02.709
Then, I will not commit adultery with another 
person's wife or husband that they got married to.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:10.600
And fourth one, I will tell the truth, 
especially about my spiritual life.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:16.840
I will not exaggerate to other 
people about my spiritual life.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.859
Number five: avoid the 
use of intoxicants and the book says,

00:07:22.430 --> 00:07:26.180
de chang le tungwa (DE CHANG LAS 'THUNG BA) or 
de dze le tungwa (DE RDZAS LAS 'THUNG BA) ??

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:39.580
means whether it's made from plants--like beer, or wine, or whiskey--or it's made from chemicals--like cocaine or things like that.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:46.660
I promise I will not use them in my life, because they make you stupid and they cost a lot of money.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:54.940
So, the full lifetime layman's vow has five parts, and

00:07:55.880 --> 00:07:58.140
Rinpoche, Pabongka Rinpoche, says, "Okay, look,

00:07:58.900 --> 00:08:05.500
forget these big monk's vows, two-hundred fifty-three vows. 
Forget the full nuns' vows, three-hundred sixty-four vows,

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:14.940
forget all these big, big, big Vinaya vows. Look, let's just talk about layman's vows. Just five vows.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:22.100
You know what? Let's talk about 
someone who says, 'Hey, I can't keep all five.'

00:08:22.340 --> 00:08:26.100
Well, can you keep any of them?
'Can you just take off the alcohol one,

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:30.224
because I like to have some wine sometimes?
Can I just keep four?'"

00:08:30.224 --> 00:08:34.420
It's called na chik na ga pel du chu (SNA GCIG SNA 'GA' 'PHEL DU SPYOD ??) in the Vinaya.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:39.400
"Okay, you can keep four," 
and then somebody says "Oh wait, wait!

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:46.900
I don't really want 
to promise to pay my taxes completely.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:51.440
Can I just take three vows?"

00:08:51.640 --> 00:08:53.680
Sorry. Oh no, I'm sorry.

00:08:53.720 --> 00:08:57.760
"I enjoy exaggerating about my meditation,

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:02.560
can I just keep these three vows: no killing, 
no stealing, no sexual misconduct?

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:06.920
that's called na sum (SNA GSUM)

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:13.560
means the guy who decided to undercommit to the five simple vows because he didn't want to take on too much.

00:09:14.060 --> 00:09:16.840
Then there's a na nyi (SNA GNYIS), what's na nyi?

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:26.260
Yeah, this guy said, "Look I'm really attracted 
to that other guy's wife or husband, can I just keep two of them?"

00:09:26.740 --> 00:09:28.468
And Buddha's like, "Yeah, okay. Okay."

00:09:28.468 --> 00:09:42.740
By the way, my lama would not give anyone less than five, but it is a tradition in ancient times to na chik na nyi na ga chu (SNA GCIG SNA GNYIS SNA 'GA' SPYOD)

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:45.880
Anyway, it is possible to give one.

00:09:46.720 --> 00:09:50.600
And then you come down to one. 
"Do you agree not to kill a human being in your life?"

00:09:50.780 --> 00:09:52.420
You say, "Okay, I can do that."

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:55.940
na chik, chi tub che--

00:09:56.300 --> 00:10:00.680
Then Rinpoche says, just do what you can do, 
just do what you can do.

00:10:00.980 --> 00:10:04.986
rab jung sok kyi tekchen sojong yang len chi tub che na--
(RAB BYUNG SOGS KYIS THEG CHEN GSO SBYONG YANG LEN CI THUB BYAS NA)

00:10:04.986 --> 00:10:11.920
And even if you have full monks vows, and 
your tantric vows, and your bodhisattva vows,

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:18.620
I don't care! If you're a person with all those vows and you get a chance to keep a one-day vow,

00:10:18.879 --> 00:10:20.050
Do it!

00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:24.400
You get a chance to take a one day vow, jump on it.

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:28.940
chi thub che na... di nyin shak chik gi dompa yinpe nampar dakpar gyurwa sok
(CI THUB BYAS NA 'DI NYIN ZHAG GCIG GI SDOM PA YIN PAS RNAM PAR DAG PAR 'GYUR BA SOGS)

00:10:29.240 --> 00:10:31.760
And then you can focus on that one-day vow.

00:10:31.900 --> 00:10:39.520
You can say, "Okay, I know I've got a hundred of these vows, tantric vows, I've got a couple hundred monk's vows,

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:43.260
I've got all these sixty-four bodhisattva vows,

00:10:43.420 --> 00:10:43.920
but

00:10:43.929 --> 00:10:47.699
I'm going to take just 
the one-day vow for dessert.

00:10:48.459 --> 00:10:52.979
I'm going to focus on that, in that one day.

00:10:53.559 --> 00:10:57.089
That's going to be my vow day for this year.

00:10:57.089 --> 00:11:03.849
I'm going to take the one-day vow once this year, 
but, I'm going to make it super special.

00:11:03.850 --> 00:11:08.540
I'm going to really, really 
work on those vows for one day.

00:11:08.540 --> 00:11:10.270
I'm going keep them so sweetly."

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:12.287
gyurwa sok gupa che
('GYUR BA SOGS DGOS PA CHE,)

00:11:12.287 --> 00:11:18.860
He says it's extremely useful, 
extremely beneficial to do that.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:22.720
rang re lapba sum sok kyi tam yang yang shu kul che mu 
(RANG RES BSLAB PA GSUM SOGS KYI GTAM YANG YANG SHOD KHUL BYED MOD,)

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:28.540
Now, guys like you and me-- 
rang ge (RANG RES) means guys "like you and me,"

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:33.120
and we said it before in the lam rim teachings, but Pabongka Rinpoche is being modest.

00:11:35.020 --> 00:11:39.560
Obviously when he says "guys like 
you and me," he means "guys like us."

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:47.640
He's just being considerate to say "people like you and me."

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:49.820
We are not like him.

00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:57.760
rang re, and especially not like his student who wrote this book down, Trijang Rinpoche, who was off the Dharma charts.

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:01.869
rang re labpa sum sok kyi tam yang yang shu--

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:08.050
You know monks, geshes, we sit around the monastery, we debate about the three trainings,

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:10.970
morality,

00:12:10.970 --> 00:12:18.020
meditation, wisdom, and you know we debate 
about it, and we blah, blah, blah about it.

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:24.620
yang yang shu kul che--we blah, blah, blah, about about these big, big trainings.

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:29.280
But he says, shen nyi ni rang gyu la suk nyen tsam yang me--
(GZHAN GNYIS NI RANG RGYUD LA GZUGS BRNYAN TZAM YANG MED)

00:12:29.540 --> 00:12:35.660
You don't have a shadow of the 
meditation and the wisdom, forget it.

00:12:36.120 --> 00:12:43.040
You don't have a single trace in your heart of the meditation and wisdom--forget those two.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:45.460
So what are you left with?

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:54.240
You got your little vows. Okay, you got your ten vows. You got your ten good deeds, focus on them.

00:12:54.440 --> 00:12:57.340
ngu su sung du yupe di la be gu--
(DNGOS SU BSRUNG DU YOD PAS 'DI LA 'BAD DGOS,)

00:12:57.340 --> 00:12:59.680
let that be your focus.

00:12:59.900 --> 00:13:04.680
Maybe you can meditate for forty-five minutes in the morning.

00:13:04.690 --> 00:13:08.799
Maybe you can listen to a Nagarjuna 
teaching if you go to the Mixed Nuts class.

00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:13.780
Or something like that. Maybe you can get it in one day.

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:19.540
But your vows, your morality, you've got that all day long.

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:23.980
You can do it all day long. 
It's always right there in your heart.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.960
So pe di la be gu (PAS 'DI LA 'BAD DGOS), means focus on that one.

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:34.640
That's always available to you, twenty-four hours a day you can be a nice person, that training is available to us.

00:13:35.170 --> 00:13:37.860
labpa sungwa la-ang tungwa jungway go dak gu
(BSLAB PA BSRUNG BA LA'ANG LTUNG BA 'BYUNG BA'I SGO DGAG DGOS,)

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:47.180
Then he says, "Look, if you want to keep your vows, keep your commitments, keep the ten or keep the sixty-four,

00:13:47.580 --> 00:13:50.140
or keep the hundred and something--

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:59.460
Your secret vows, your bodhisattva vows--if you want to keep them, there's three ways to break them."

00:13:59.460 --> 00:14:04.020
There's three ways to... it's called 
the door to break your vows.

00:14:04.020 --> 00:14:09.500
There's three doors to break your vows.
It's a very famous thing in the scriptures.

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:13.380
There's three doors to break your vows.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:21.060
Your vows can start leaking if 
there's three things open in your heart.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:28.560
Three things--three caps--
that are supposed to be closed.

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:36.080
Three caps that are supposed to be closed in your heart and, if they get loose, you will break your vows.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:41.760
The green drink will spill all over the nice white couch.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:46.220
So there's three jar tops 
you have to be careful with.

00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:48.440
Here's the three.

00:14:48.840 --> 00:14:50.100
Number one.

00:14:50.260 --> 00:14:57.760
Then we see here a chef, and 
I think he looks a little confused.

00:14:57.760 --> 00:15:06.300
Like I like to cook for my partner Veronica and she insists that I study the recipe before I try to cook it.

00:15:06.300 --> 00:15:12.740
Then I like to say, "Look, I've been cooking my whole... 
I was the monastery cook for eight years,

00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:16.900
I know how to cook and we don't read 
cookbooks in the monastery.

00:15:16.960 --> 00:15:22.360
We just cook." And she's like, "Read the recipe." I'm like, "I don't have to read the recipe."

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:28.040
Then she just really insisted, and to make peace in our home,

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:36.840
especially during the lockdown, I said, "Listen, okay, I will read the recipe. I will follow the recipe."

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:41.920
So, there are four ways that your vows can leak.

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:53.340
There's four ways to put the top on crooked and things are going to get messy on the white couch with the green drink if that, if that's loose.

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:56.160
Four different ways. We're going to cover them.

00:15:56.760 --> 00:16:00.920
We'll do three in this episode and 
we'll do one in the next episode, I think.

00:16:02.280 --> 00:16:03.960
So number one.

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:12.280
Read the recipe. Number one is, 
if you want to keep your vows and you 
want to keep your commitments, read the recipe.

00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:15.920
For fifty dollars, what's it mean?

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:18.160
Read the recipe?

00:16:21.840 --> 00:16:23.840
What?

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.580
Tim?

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:36.000
Read the recipe? No, okay. I guess, he says the first way, the first trick to keeping your vows is to read the recipe.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.220
What's it mean?

00:16:41.160 --> 00:16:43.279
Learn the instructions.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:48.280
Like, when I was the young and stupid--

00:16:48.280 --> 00:16:57.600
now I'm old and stupid--but when I was young 
and stupid, people said, "We're going to an 
initiation, the big lama is going to give initiation."

00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:02.220
I'm like, "I'm there man. I'm there. I want to go."

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:06.300
I don't know, I was more 
wanting to hang out with my friends,

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:11.900
take a trip on a plane or hang out with my friends. 
But I said, "Yeah, I'm there.

00:17:11.900 --> 00:17:17.440
I'm going. I'm going to the initiation." 
Then there'd be these lamas, they're ringing bells

00:17:18.000 --> 00:17:21.860
"buhbuh, buhbuh, buhbuh," and 
then they go "waaaaaa" and "bung, bung, bung,"

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:23.520
"chung, chung, chung."

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:31.720
And I was like, "Wow, this is cool. 
This is amazing. Look at that bell."

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:38.000
And then "waaaaa." I'm like, "Wow, this is a real blessing."

00:17:38.580 --> 00:17:46.340
Then I'd go home, back to the monastery, and my teacher would say, "I heard you got a tantric initiation."

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:49.460
I'd said, "Yeah. Wow, that was a lama! That was a high Lama."

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:54.680
He said, "Well, yes. So are you going to keep those vows?

00:17:55.620 --> 00:18:02.300
Because that's that's how the empowerment works. 
If you keep the vows that they gave you during the empowerment,

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:06.859
then magic happens in your life. Then magic will happen in your life."

00:18:07.260 --> 00:18:12.079
Then he said, "Are you going to keep the vows?" 
I'm like, "What vows?"

00:18:12.420 --> 00:18:18.499
He says, "They gave you an empowerment and they didn't give the vows?" I'm like, 
"I don't know--it was all in another language.

00:18:18.500 --> 00:18:23.869
I guess they gave me the vows." 
"What?! They gave you vows, they didn't tell you what the vows are?

00:18:24.020 --> 00:18:29.240
How do you think that tantra is going to work 
if you don't follow the vows?

00:18:29.280 --> 00:18:37.100
It doesn't work. The magic doesn't happen if you don't keep the vows and they didn't even teach you the vows." 
I'm like, "No."

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:42.960
Okay, so number one law:

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:50.220
You can't keep your vows if you don't 
know what the vows are. It's so funny.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:55.880
The vows are the machine that 
drives the magic of Buddhism.

00:18:56.220 --> 00:19:00.980
The vows are the machine that drives the Tesla car.

00:19:01.620 --> 00:19:14.520
The vows are the solar battery of this sports car 
and if you don't even know them, then 
it's hopeless; you will just break them.

00:19:15.440 --> 00:19:21.760
Your life will get unmagical because you broke them, 
the initiation vows, because no one taught them to you.

00:19:21.760 --> 00:19:28.060
I think we should all go on strike, 
all of us normal people should go on strike.

00:19:28.060 --> 00:19:32.030
We should refuse to attend an empowerment 
if the lama doesn't teach us the vows.

00:19:32.030 --> 00:19:35.992
Then we should say, "On strike." 
"Are you going to teach vows?"

00:19:35.992 --> 00:19:39.769
"No, I don't have time. 
I have to be in California next week."

00:19:40.320 --> 00:19:45.380
"Okay, then I'm going home. 
I'm not taking this empowerment."

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:48.860
I think that would be really a good idea.

00:19:49.100 --> 00:19:50.640
So here,

00:19:50.640 --> 00:19:53.080
dangpo mi shepa tungwa jungway go yin pe--
(DANG PO MI SHES PA LTUNG BA 'BYUNG BA'I SGO YIN PAS)

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:58.291
Not knowing what vows you took 
is the number one way to break them.

00:19:58.291 --> 00:20:01.460
kakpa ni (BKAG PA NI)--if you want to stop that,

00:20:02.340 --> 00:20:04.970
lab shi gangshik sung gupa ma she na
(BSLAB GZHI GANG ZHIG BSRUNG DGOS PA MA SHES NA,)

00:20:06.960 --> 00:20:10.400
If you don't know the vows that 
you're supposed to be keeping,

00:20:10.560 --> 00:20:11.880
tungwa jung ma jung mi she
(LTUNG BA BYUNG MA BYUNG MI SHES)

00:20:11.900 --> 00:20:15.100
Then you're not going to know 
whether you've broke it or not. Duh!

00:20:15.809 --> 00:20:17.490
mi shes (MI SHES)...

00:20:17.490 --> 00:20:20.440
lo dang tun te (BLO DANG BSTUN TE)

00:20:21.000 --> 00:20:24.440
Then he says third. Yeah, that's right Seiji, third line,

00:20:25.020 --> 00:20:26.986
lo dang tun te is very funny.

00:20:26.986 --> 00:20:35.740
He says, "You should be studying those vows 
from the great books as far as you can read them."

00:20:36.000 --> 00:20:40.600
He's making fun of us. 
"I know you guys can't read Vinaya,

00:20:41.490 --> 00:20:43.490
but,

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:46.720
just give it a try--okay?--as much as you can."

00:20:47.020 --> 00:20:48.400
lo dang tun

00:20:48.600 --> 00:20:59.340
It's basically saying, "I know you guys are too lazy to crack the Vinaya sutras and study them, but can you do a little bit?

00:20:59.480 --> 00:21:02.120
Can you make a little bit of effort 
to learn what your vows are?"

00:21:03.160 --> 00:21:06.320
dulway shung chenmo dak gam
('DUL BA'I GZHUNG CHEN MO DAG GAM,)

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:13.340
You could study the great books of Vinaya, which are difficult. Or, if that's too hard for you,

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:15.480
lap jay dom tsik
(BSLAB BYA'I SDOM TSIG,)

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:19.880
There are little poems that they write about Vinaya. You can study one of those poems.

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:23.140
shi sum lab ja
(GZHI GSUM BSLAB BYA,)

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:30.100
There's tiny, tiny poems about 
the three foundations of morality.

00:21:30.380 --> 00:21:38.800
The three foundations of morality for a monk 
or a nun are to do your confession twice a month,

00:21:39.140 --> 00:21:43.780
to do your summer retreat so you 
don't destroy the environment,

00:21:44.200 --> 00:21:50.040
and then the best one is ga ye (DGAG DBYE), 
which is the end of the summer retreat

00:21:50.480 --> 00:21:56.500
when you're allowed to play rock &amp; roll in the monastery for twenty-four hours or something.

00:21:57.059 --> 00:21:59.329
All the monks observe this one very well.

00:22:02.550 --> 00:22:07.039
And we all play games and it's really fun.

00:22:07.760 --> 00:22:12.320
So at least study those three 
things you're supposed to be doing.

00:22:12.820 --> 00:22:14.320
lung shiy bar dom
(LUNG GZHI'I BAR SDOMS)

00:22:14.540 --> 00:22:22.580
There's summaries of the Vinaya Vastu, 
the foundation of morality.

00:22:23.220 --> 00:22:27.520
Read those little summaries. 
They have little poems in them,

00:22:27.520 --> 00:22:30.560
between the big sections, so they're called bar dom (BAR SDOMS)--

00:22:31.880 --> 00:22:33.799
you get an intermission.

00:22:33.799 --> 00:22:35.799
Intermission Vinaya books.

00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:41.120
te ne che tsam nam kyi drang dren tsun che shespar che
(BLTAS NAS BCAS MTSAMS RNAMS KYI GRANGS 'DREN TSUN CHAD SHES PAR BYED,)

00:22:41.280 --> 00:22:43.600
At least be able to count your vows.

00:22:44.360 --> 00:22:49.913
dak tu shen mu chu nor mi ter zhin, shak kyang mi nyen tekchen pongwa dang,
konchok kor trok chu pong ngur mik trok, tsam me nga dang lok ta dru sok jom, 
ma jang tongnyi ten dang dzok jang dok, so tar pong dang nyen mu sab dzun ma...

00:22:49.913 --> 00:22:52.135
(BDAG BSTOD GZHAN SMOD CHOS NOR MI STER ZHING,
,BSHAGS KYANG MI NYAN THEG CHEN SPONG BA DANG,

00:22:52.135 --> 00:22:54.548
,DKON MCHOG DKOR 'PHROG CHOS SPONG NGUR SMRIG 'PHROG 
,MTSAMS MED LNGA DANG LOG LTA GROD SOGS 'JOMS,

00:22:54.548 --> 00:22:56.960
,MA SBYANGS STONG NYID BSTAN DANG RDZOGS BYANG LDOG 
,SO THAR SPONG DANG NYAN SMOD ZAB BRDZUN SMRA,)

00:22:57.260 --> 00:22:59.960
Like that. At least be able to count your vows.

00:23:00.560 --> 00:23:04.340
Start with that. If you can't count them, 
you can't keep them.

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:07.580
That's the first obstacle to keeping your vows.

00:23:08.299 --> 00:23:10.299
What was it again?

00:23:10.700 --> 00:23:14.700
No one ever taught them to you. "Oh, my god!

00:23:15.640 --> 00:23:22.540
They sold you a Tesla without the engine, 
without the solar battery!" It's funny.

00:23:22.880 --> 00:23:27.020
Second one: ma gupa tungwa jungway go yin pe
(MA GUS PA LTUNG BA 'BYUNG BA'I SGO YIN PAS)

00:23:27.520 --> 00:23:31.180
ma gupa (MA GUS PA) means, again, you blow off these vows.

00:23:31.520 --> 00:23:32.360
"Come on,

00:23:32.600 --> 00:23:38.600
I'm not supposed to blow my nose on a green leaf? Come on?"

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:43.520
That's called not honoring your vows.

00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:47.240
There's a French monk. Matthieu Ricard,

00:23:48.620 --> 00:23:53.259
I heard about a TV show he was on 
and he's a great writer and a great monk.

00:23:54.360 --> 00:23:55.000
He said...

00:23:56.380 --> 00:24:03.980
Somebody said--the interviewer said--"Don't you feel constrained by your vows, all these vows,

00:24:04.480 --> 00:24:07.980
they make you feel like you're in a straight jacket, right?

00:24:08.239 --> 00:24:12.129
Don't you feel like you're in a straight jacket?"
And he looked at the guy and he said,

00:24:13.420 --> 00:24:22.260
"Those vows are wings that I use to fly. Those vows are not a strait jacket, those vows are my flying wings.

00:24:22.820 --> 00:24:27.560
When I have vows and when I keep vows, man, I can fly."

00:24:28.930 --> 00:24:33.140
To blow off the vows and say 
"Oh those are not so important."

00:24:33.140 --> 00:24:36.080
dey chepa dang, drok tsangpa tsungpar chupa nam la gupa dang
(DE'I BCAS PA DANG, GROGS TSANGS PA MTSUNGS PAR SPYOD PA RNAMS LA GUS PA DANG,)

00:24:36.080 --> 00:24:36.760
Also,

00:24:37.180 --> 00:24:43.820
part of respecting the vows is to show respect 
to the people who are keeping them well.

00:24:44.400 --> 00:24:53.360
So you respect your vows on paper, but also respective vows as your friends are keeping them.

00:24:53.920 --> 00:25:01.740
Like Seiji starts pulling out his six-times book and Geshe-la's embarrassed, because he's not keeping his.

00:25:03.970 --> 00:25:09.179
Then respect the vows as other people are 
keeping them and that's another kind of 
respect you can show your vows.

00:25:10.120 --> 00:25:19.460
Respect your friends when they keep their vows, and that's  a very powerful force for keeping your own vows.

00:25:19.840 --> 00:25:24.900
gupa che, hlakpar rang gyu kyi labpa la tunpa sanggye kyi dushe shak
(GUS PA BYED, LHAG PAR RANG RGYUD KYI BSLAB PA LA STON PA SANGS RGYAS KYI 'DU SHES BZHAG)

00:25:25.600 --> 00:25:31.320
Don't forget that the vows in your 
heart are the Buddha himself.

00:25:31.320 --> 00:25:36.160
Buddha said, "If you keep the vows in 
your heart, then I am living in your heart."

00:25:37.990 --> 00:25:39.869
shak ching gupa che
(BZHAG CING GUS PA BYED)

00:25:39.869 --> 00:25:44.860
Respect those vows in your own heart as 
if the Buddha is sitting in your own heart.

00:25:44.860 --> 00:25:47.740
You can prostrate to your heart sometimes.

00:25:48.960 --> 00:25:50.960
de la nang chung mi ja
(DE LA MNANGS CHUNG MI BYA)

00:25:51.300 --> 00:25:58.760
Don't do nang chung (MNANGS CHUNG). nang chung is a very, very rare colloquial word and it means

00:25:58.860 --> 00:26:06.480
don't fall into the trap of thinking some of 
those vows are not so important, or not so sexy.

00:26:06.480 --> 00:26:07.980
Don't think like that.

00:26:08.740 --> 00:26:17.100
Don't think some vows are super sexy and very mystical, and some vows are just kind of small practical things.

00:26:17.820 --> 00:26:19.740
that's nang chung.

00:26:19.750 --> 00:26:22.530
Making that distinction is called nang chung.

00:26:23.380 --> 00:26:27.330
tunpa nyengen lende je kyi ku tsab tabu yin
(STON PA MYA NGAN LAS 'DAS RJES KYI SKU TSAB LTA BU YIN,)

00:26:29.800 --> 00:26:37.140
When the Buddha left his world, this world, 
he left behind a representative,

00:26:37.340 --> 00:26:42.700
his representative, to remind people about his time here.

00:26:43.160 --> 00:26:47.960
That representative is the 
vows that have been passed on

00:26:47.960 --> 00:26:52.200
from generation to generation 
for the last two and a half thousand years.

00:26:52.560 --> 00:26:59.640
So respect the Buddha in the form of the vows 
in your heart and in the heart of other people.

00:26:59.800 --> 00:27:00.440
Okay, cool.

00:27:00.740 --> 00:27:05.330
We're done with that episode and I'll see you at episode six.

00:27:06.150 --> 00:27:09.379
Thank you. And thanks Seiji and Tim for help.

